kind: AdaptiveDialog
startBehavior: CancelOtherTopics
inputs:
  - kind: AutomaticTaskInput
    propertyName: CaseSubject
    description: |-
      A short, customer-friendly title for this service case, written in plain business English, maximum 80 characters.
      Describe what the caller actually needs, for example "Question about lease-end return options" or "Dispute over a late payment fee".
      Never mention transfers, escalation, specialists, agents, IVR, bots, systems, tools, phone numbers, or conversation IDs.
    shouldPromptUser: false

  - kind: AutomaticTaskInput
    propertyName: CaseSummary
    description: |-
      A concise plain-English summary of this conversation for the person who will take the call, written as 2 to 4 natural sentences.
      Cover what the caller asked about, the details they gave such as vehicle, account, amounts or dates, what was already explained to them, and what still needs to be resolved.
      Write it the way a helpful colleague would write a handover note.
      Never include phone numbers, conversation IDs, tool names, technical terms, or any mention of transfer or escalation mechanics.
    shouldPromptUser: false

